cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
title: "ConvNeXt V2 + FCMAE from scratch, on blood cell microscopy"
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch PyTorch implementation of the ConvNeXt V2 encoder and a masked
  autoencoder pre-training pipeline, applied to five-class blood cell
  classification. Originally a graduate course project reporting 94.8% test
  accuracy, it was re-opened and re-evaluated with the controls the original
  submission never ran: a from-scratch baseline, a linear probe, a random-feature
  control, a label-budget sweep, and three seeds throughout. The controls show
  that the self-supervised pre-training is a wash at full label budgets, that the
  pre-trained encoder is a worse frozen feature extractor than a randomly
  initialised one, and that a 48-dimensional colour histogram with logistic
  regression reaches 94.4% on the same test set — matching the deep model without
  any morphological understanding.
